.TH IPV6DDNS 1 "" ipv6ddns "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ipv6ddns \- DNS names for every device on your network, wherever its addresses move
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ipv6ddns
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIfile\fR]
[\fB\-\-live\fR]
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ipv6ddns discovers the hosts of the network, with their addresses and names, and keeps the addresses of those its configuration chooses, IPv6 and IPv4, in the records of a DNS provider. It updates a name when its addresses change.
.PP
It runs until it is stopped. On SIGINT or SIGTERM the updates in progress get up to 30 seconds to finish, and a second signal stops it at once.
.PP
Local discovery needs raw sockets: root, or the CAP_NET_RAW capability.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fIfile\fR
The configuration file, YAML or JSON: the names to keep, the providers, the discovery, the level of the log and the web server. Without it: config.yaml, or /etc/ipv6ddns/config.yaml, the first there is.
.TP
\fB\-\-live\fR
Show the state in the terminal, updating, instead of the log.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Show the version, and exit.
.PP
Everything else is in the configuration file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config.yaml
The configuration, without \fB\-\-config\fR: the working directory's.
.TP
.I /etc/ipv6ddns/config.yaml
The configuration, when the one before is not there: the system's, as a package installs it.
.SH SEE ALSO
The keys of the configuration file:
.UR https://github.com/miguelangel-nubla/ipv6ddns/blob/main/docs/reference/configuration.md
.UE
